{"data":{"list":[{"author":"claude","cmd":"type","facet":"command","label":"delete command type","new":"","old":"{\"command\":{\"name\":\"type\",\"rust\":\"myqqrj1a03b81320et12\",\"type\":\"rust\"},\"impl\":{\"attachmentkeynames\":[\"rs\"],\"import\":\"use ndata::dataobject::DataObject;\",\"params\":[{\"name\":\"selector\",\"type\":\"String\"},{\"name\":\"value\",\"type\":\"String\"}],\"returntype\":\"JSONObject\",\"rs\":\"// Set the value of the first element matching `selector` to `value` and\\n// fire input+change events (so page frameworks notice). value is true\\n// when the element was found. {status, value}.\\nfn js_string(s: &str) -> String {\\n    let mut out = String::from(\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\");\\n    for c in s.chars() {\\n        match c {\\n            '\\\"' => out.push_str(\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\"),\\n            '\\\\\\\\' => out.push_str(\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"),\\n            '\\\\n' => out.push_str(\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\"),\\n            '\\\\r' => out.push_str(\\\"\\\\\\\\r\\\"),\\n            '\\\\t' => out.push_str(\\\"\\\\\\\\t\\\"),\\n            c if (c as u32) < 0x20 => out.push_str(&format!(\\\"\\\\\\\\u{:04x}\\\", c as u32)),\\n            c => out.push(c),\\n        }\\n    }\\n    out.push('\\\"');\\n    out\\n}\\nlet js = format!(\\n    \\\"(function(){{var e=document.querySelector({});if(!e)return false;e.focus();e.value={};e.dispatchEvent(new Event('input',{{bubbles:true}}));e.dispatchEvent(new Event('change',{{bubbles:true}}));return true;}})()\\\",\\n    js_string(&selector),\\n    js_string(&value)\\n);\\ncrate::agent::browser::eval::eval(js, 5000)\",\"type\":\"rust\"}}","patch_id":"p1","time":1787704727477},{"author":"promote","cmd":"","facet":"memory","label":"promote: fold -> agent.browser","new":"[\n{\"claim\": \"Noobscape v2 injection is bound to ONE tab: the first top-level content docshell at the launch URL latches by writing its top browsing-context id to bind.id (O_CREAT|O_EXCL), and thereafter only the matching top docshell answers inject requests - all others stay silent, QUIT bypasses the gate and clears bind.id.\", \"detail\": \"Fix for the random-docshell race where any frame could eat an eval. open() clears bind.id and writes bind.url (trailing-slash-normalized match); close() removes both. Per-process dedup runs AFTER the gate so a subframe sharing the tab's process cannot eat a top-document request. Verified headless: a per-window counter returned 1->2->3 across three evals on the same window. Incremental rebuild of the one-file nsDocShell.cpp change is ~36s.\", \"tags\": \"agent.browser,agent.browser_builder,noobscape,nsDocShell,bind-latch,unreviewed\", \"confidence\": \"high\", \"time\": 1787772695336},\n{\"claim\": \"Script-initiated navigation never commits from Noobscape v2 eval: goto(), location.href= and location.assign() all run (the JS returns) but the page never changes - same-origin, cross-origin, and about:blank alike; only open()'s command-line URL loads.\", \"detail\": \"Found 2026-08-26 while verifying the bind latch; NOT caused by the latch (the gate is not in the navigation path, and the latch kept answering from the same live document throughout). Leading hypothesis: the mechanism evaluates with AutoJSAPI, which lacks the entry-script settings a script-initiated navigation requires - the candidate fix is AutoEntryScript(innerWindow, \\\"Noobscape\\\", true). Unresolved pending owner go-ahead.\", \"tags\": \"agent.browser,agent.browser_builder,noobscape,navigation,AutoJSAPI,AutoEntryScript,unreviewed\", \"confidence\": \"high\", \"time\": 1787772700759, \"adjudicated\": 1787774523434, \"corroborations\": 1},\n{\"claim\": \"No in-page screenshot route exists in Noobscape; Firefox's own --headless --screenshot launcher is the working capture path, and under the rebind navigation model it is equivalent to shooting the live tab.\", \"detail\": \"drawWindow was removed in Fission-era Firefox and content-process pixel capture is unreachable from the injected script, so eval cannot render the page to a canvas. What works is launching firefox --headless --screenshot against a throwaway profile - the same CLI mechanism open() trusts. It shoots a URL rather than the driven tab, but since navigation is already rebind-per-goto, 'screenshot this URL' and 'screenshot the current tab' are the same thing in practice. Verified: valid 1280x1000 PNG (385KB) of Wikipedia. No dedicated screenshot command exists yet - candidate for agent.browser.screenshot.\", \"tags\": \"agent.browser,noobscape,screenshot,firefox,headless,unreviewed\", \"confidence\": \"high\", \"time\": 1787774528349},\n{\"claim\": \"A leftover QUIT sentinel in NOOBSCAPE_DIR/inject.js ambushes every later Firefox launch on that channel: the mechanism is compiled into the binary, so any new process (a screenshot run, a hand launch) reads the stale QUIT at startup and force-quits itself mid-boot.\", \"detail\": \"Bisected from a 90s screenshot hang; the log showed 'Noobscape: force quitting...' during boot. Driver-side fixes, no rebuild: screenshot launches with NOOBSCAPE_DIR pointed at an empty throwaway dir so its watcher can never collide with the live channel, and close() now deletes the consumed inject.js along with the other channel files so a QUIT cannot outlive its session.\", \"tags\": \"agent.browser,noobscape,firefox,gotcha,unreviewed\", \"confidence\": \"high\", \"time\": 1787776306548},\n{\"end\": true}]\n","old":"","patch_id":"p2","time":1787783297639}]},"id":"nnyhjm1a03b7e0f6ex6_patches","readers":[],"time":1787783297639,"username":"system","writers":[]}